[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5134638884","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121950#issuecomment-5134638884","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121950","id":5134638884,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMgxfJA","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-30T18:17:34Z","updated_at":"2026-07-30T18:17:34Z","body":"This is expected, since editor have both `es_AR` and `es` it will select best match. Currently, multiple translations are never mixed, only one is used at the time. But I guess it might make sense to fall back to the more generic one for missing strings.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5134638884/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5134687061","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121950#issuecomment-5134687061","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121950","id":5134687061,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMg0bVQ","user":{"login":"manuq","id":83944,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzOTQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83944?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/manuq","html_url":"https://github.com/manuq","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manuq/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manuq/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manuq/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manuq/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manuq/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manuq/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manuq/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manuq/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manuq/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-30T18:21:55Z","updated_at":"2026-07-30T18:22:09Z","body":"> This is expected, since editor have both `es_AR` and `es` it will select best match. Currently, multiple translations are never mixed, only one is used at the time. But I guess it might make sense to fall back to the more generic one for missing strings.\n\nYes that is what I would expect considering how Gettext works. Gettext country-specific locale fallbacks automatically by stripping the regional code (in my case `es_AR` goes down to `es`) and finally to the default domain text.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5134687061/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5135440117","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121950#issuecomment-5135440117","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121950","id":5135440117,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMhiY9Q","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-30T19:37:52Z","updated_at":"2026-07-30T19:37:52Z","body":"> Currently, multiple translations are never mixed, only one is used at the time. \n\nActually this is not true in the current version, seems like it's just not loading both locales, but everything necessary to fallback like this is in the engine, so it should be really easy to implement. I'll check it tomorrow.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5135440117/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5219155857","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121950#issuecomment-5219155857","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121950","id":5219155857,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNxX_kQ","user":{"login":"noidexe","id":526829,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNjgyOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/526829?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/noidexe","html_url":"https://github.com/noidexe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noidexe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noidexe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noidexe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noidexe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noidexe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noidexe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noidexe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noidexe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noidexe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-07T15:49:14Z","updated_at":"2026-08-07T15:49:29Z","body":"What's the process to deprecate/drop a translation?\n\nI created es_AR back when Godot didn't have any Spanish translation. I had the time to quickly translate the engine to my regional dialect, but  researching about all the regional differences, especially in how technical terms were translated (or if at all) was beyond my time and knowledge. \nSo in the beginning `es` was just a mirror of `es_AR` waiting for translators from other regions, but now there's a team of translators from several countries and after discussing with members of the Argentine community everyone agrees the base `es` translation is pretty good. \n\nI no longer have time to take care of `es_AR` and my attempts to find volunteers have so far been unsuccessful, so I think it's safe to deprecate/drop the regional translation. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5219155857/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5221548427","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121950#issuecomment-5221548427","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121950","id":5221548427,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNzqBiw","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-07T20:09:40Z","updated_at":"2026-08-07T20:10:50Z","body":"\n> I no longer have time to take care of `es_AR` and my attempts to find volunteers have so far been unsuccessful, so I think it's safe to deprecate/drop the regional translation.\n\nWe can do multiple things:\n- Fully delete it from Weblate and from the Godot repo\n- Keep it on Weblate if some contributors still want to work on finalizing it, but change our scripts to skip es_AR.po when pushing changes to Godot\n\nOverall, I'd favor the first option, as I believe even if new contributors were motivated to maintain a regional variant, it might be better to start from a new copy of `es` and then do regional adaptations (I would imagine a bunch of it would be glossary find and replace).\n\nBut maybe we can start by locking `es_AR` on Weblate and put a message there to direct people to #translation-es on RC if they want to discuss continuing the work on this variant.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5221548427/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]